<title>USA: Green Mountain seeks 16.7 pct rate increase.</title>
<headline>Green Mountain seeks 16.7 pct rate increase.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH BURLINGTON, Vt. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green Mountain Power Corp said on Monday that it had asked the Vermont Public Service Board to authorize a 16.7 percent rate increase, in part to cover the rising cost of power purchased under contracts with Hydro-Quebec.</p>
<p>GMP said it needed $26 million in additional revenues in 1998, with about 70 percent of the increase required to meet rising power supply cost commitments. In 1998, GMP's cost for Hydro-Quebec power will be $17 million more than in 1997, the electric utility said in a statement.</p>
</text>
